\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The four image encodings of one triaxial WISDM walking window, with the per-axis $(x,y,z)$ intensities stacked as the RGB channels. RP encodes signed recurrence distances between adjacent states; GASF is symmetric; GADF is antisymmetric and therefore directional; and MTF shows the discrete transition-level regions of its quantised states. RP is $127\times 127$ (adjacent-state embedding) and the others $128\times 128$. The reconstructions of this same window are shown in Figure~\ref {fig:qualitative_main}.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:encodings_main}{{2}{3}{}{}{}}
